+The preceding October 14 repair's run creation to main-model dispatch took 5.51/7.22 seconds in the browser and 7.19/8.98 seconds in the CLI. Dispatch to processed first text took 0.57–0.71 seconds; private recall took 2.34–4.57 seconds. Actual selected context remained within the published input bound: one or three messages, two to four memories, zero to two facts and zero or one pending entry. The response model and Gateway's internal network subdivisions are not separately observable. Cortex preparation, retrieval and protected delivery still require further work; these separate clocks are not additive.
+
+Its approved memory tool and final answer completed after one approval, including an observer disconnect/reconnect. A separate repeated-exchange test passed 221 native provenance checks, contiguous facts/vectors through four messages, public recall and the original access, lock, deletion and revocation negatives. That public recall took 2.79 seconds. These results do not accept every chat memory outcome: two ordinary user events failed validation because one extraction duplicated a fact slot and another returned malformed tags. Later successful events correctly remained behind those watermark holes. The disposable database, container and private credentials were independently verified absent after testing.
