+
+Both clients returned their requested ordinary replies. Earlier candidates passed the eight-event native memory check. V7 completed contiguous indexing through all eight events and passed the individual source/vector/usage checks, but its original fact-attribution check failed: only one of four user events had a fresh attributed fact. Two question turns produced no facts; the declaration turn's missing attribution remains unexplained. The complete memory verifier remains FAIL. The browser was signed out and closed before the CLI samples, and each disposable database and container was verified absent after testing. These are separate empty/populated-context conditions, not a controlled comparison with a historical release. The latency target remains unmet.
+
+V7's main answer dispatch started 2.76/2.72 seconds after run creation in the browser and 6.30/11.21 seconds in the CLI. Processed first model text followed 0.46–0.68 seconds later. CLI recall took 3.12/6.06 seconds, with actual budget-account and foreground run-row conflicts. A separate authenticated public `memory.recall` returned the correct nine results in 4.79 seconds; its final delivery transaction alone took 2.21 seconds and read 998 documents. These measurements identify repeated validation/read work and transaction contention before inference. They do not expose Gateway internal routing or provider queue timing.
+
+The V7 tool request failed before its first answer-model call: the unchanged conservative input bound computed 34,938 against a configured 32,768 limit. This is an accounting ceiling, not a provider token measurement. No approval or tool effect occurred. The user has authorized bounded context selection to address request growth while retaining the complete canonical transcript and these model limits. The subsequent bounded-context candidate passed the separately measured tool continuation. That result does not repair any historical failed sample.
+
