+## 5. Submit and observe
+
+Use [`submitAndStart`](../api-reference/runtime-client.mdx#combined-admission-and-recovery) with a retained caller request ID to admit new text and request streaming execution. The result contains the handle, current run and start metadata; observe the handle for the answer rather than issuing a second model call. Existing `submit`/`start` remain available for explicit approval and recovery. An unknown outcome requires inspecting the original request/run, not automatic redispatch with a new identity.
+
+In the canonical Basic app, plain text generates and prints one request ID, submits the turn, and watches/displays streamed output plus the canonical final answer through the same client. `/send <requestId> <text>` returns the handle for later `/observe` or `/watch`; it does not wait to display the answer. Ctrl+C closes local observation, while `/cancel` asks the backend to cancel. Response completion can precede asynchronous memory readiness, and optional title work follows canonical answer finalization.
+
+The current local release candidates are SDK/CLI/provider 0.39.0, Basic app payload 1.4.1, Vercel quickstart app payload 1.4.2, and the independently versioned templates catalog 1.3.2. These versions do not claim registry publication.
+
+## Optional latency diagnostics
+
+For an authorized backend, enable `CORTEX_RUNTIME_LATENCY_TRACE=1` in that backend's environment to record scalar context, model-policy, Gateway and finalization phase metadata. The Basic CLI uses the same flag in its own process for client RPC and submission-to-first-printed-answer markers. The Vercel quickstart uses `NEXT_PUBLIC_CORTEX_LATENCY_TRACE=1` for SDK events and browser DOM-commit/after-paint markers; set it in the app environment before building/running the app.
+
+These opt-in flags do not contain prompts, output text or credentials. [Performance measurement](../architecture/performance.mdx#latency-diagnostics) explains the clock domains and visibility boundaries. Submission to first visible text under one second is a target; current measurements must establish whether a particular deployment meets it.
+
 ## Optional capabilities
 
 Configure [graph workers](../advanced-topics/graph-integration.mdx) when graph projection is required. [Private assets and media](../core-features/assets-and-media.mdx) use the configured HTTP origin and retained jobs. The media guide covers service access, supported inputs and saved-operation recovery.
